leed 1 curse die; Ethereal, Lineage (Dead)<br /> Portal; Hold 2 curse dice; Ethereal, Lineage (Nephilim)<br /> Telekinesis; Bleed 1 curse die; Ethereal, Lineage (Dead)<br /> Teleport; Bleed 1 curse dice; Ethereal<br /> <br /> <b>Thaumaturgy</b><br /> Bombardment; Bleed 1 curse dice; Elemental, Lineage (Get of Lyka)<br /> Alter Fate; Bleed 1 curse die; Emotional, Ethereal<br /> Elemental Armor; Bleed 1 curse die; Physical, Elemental, Lineage (Outcasts), Support<br /> Summon Imp; Bleed 1 curse die; Elemental, Physical, Lineage (Outcasts), Support<br /> Time Warp; Bleed 1 curse die; Ethereal, Support<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T15:04:47-07:00","id":1544752,"title":"","content":"Wow, that\u2019s great, good work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T15:10:27-07:00","id":1544754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544683-lineage-spell-list?p=1544752#post1544752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that\u2019s great, good work!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. My next plan is to go through all the Families and look at what spells actually benefit from their Motifs. I think it's mostly pretty ... balanced isn't the word because this isn't a &quot;balance&quot; type of game but pretty flexible, although I think the Zeds get a bit screwed on theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T19:26:22-07:00","id":1544766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544683-lineage-spell-list?p=1544754#post1544754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No problem. My next plan is to go through all the Families and look at what spells actually benefit from their Motifs. I think it's mostly pretty ... balanced isn't the word because this isn't a &quot;balance&quot; type of game but pretty flexible, although I think the Zeds get a bit screwed on theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome. I haven\u2019t play tested anything yet, but I\u2019m thinking I really like the motifs that reduce the amount of Curse Dice that you have to bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T04:41:23-07:00","id":1544787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544683-lineage-spell-list?p=1544766#post1544766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be awesome. I haven\u2019t play tested anything yet, but I\u2019m thinking I really like the motifs that reduce the amount of Curse Dice that you have to bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't based on actual play experience but I'm currently quite concerned that the &quot;bleed fewer Curse Dice&quot; motives are distortingly more effective than the others. Like I'd 100% always make that Motif my first pick and I'd honestly hesitate to play a Family that didn't have access to one.<br /> <br /> I know this game (quite correctly) doesn't worry about white room balance, but for example if one Motif lets you bleed an extra CD to have a Spell affect an extra target then while that *is* useful the character who took the reduction Motif can just cast the same spell twice.<br /> <br /> Motifs are also kind of unbalanced in how many spells they affect, with at least one, by my reading, affecting literally none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T01:35:11-07:00","id":1544834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544683-lineage-spell-list?p=1544787#post1544787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't based on actual play experience but I'm currently quite concerned that the &quot;bleed fewer Curse Dice&quot; motives are distortingly more effective than the others. Like I'd 100% always make that Motif my first pick and I'd honestly hesitate to play a Family that didn't have access to one.<br /> <br /> I know this game (quite correctly) doesn't worry about white room balance, but for example if one Motif lets you bleed an extra CD to have a Spell affect an extra target then while that *is* useful the character who took the reduction Motif can just cast the same spell twice.<br /> <br /> Motifs are also kind of unbalanced in how many spells they affect, with at least one, by my reading, affecting literally none.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that myself, though I wondered if it was my own bias of really liking spells that can be cast without limit. <br /> <br /> I think it would be nice if every family had a motif that reduced bleed cost.<br /> <br /> I noticed in some cases, a family reduced the bleed cost of physical spells and there are oodles of physical spells with bleed requirements.<br /> <br /> The Chimera, on the other hand, can reduce bleed costs on summoning - which means unlimited imps and eventually unlimited ranged magical attacks - but it\u2019s still very limited in comparison","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T04:44:19-07:00","id":1544836,"title":"","content":"Obviously it's possible that we just have similar biases but I feel like it can't be *that* uncommon for people to feel unlimited magic is better than costly special effects. Hell I've even listened to an episode of the pathcast where one of the devs talks about how impactful a free spell can be.<br /> <br /> Of course a lot of it will depend on the Curse Dice economy but everything I've seen from APs suggests that characters gain CDs very rarely and only bleed down to 0 in an emergency, meaning characters without cost reduction effects just kinda don't use much magic.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I'd go so far as to say every family should have one; that might get samey but I think it might at least be worth trying. Between Affinities, Practises, and less clearly defined conditionals (when you cast a spell on somebody you have a bond with, when you cast a spell on yourself etc) it should be doable without repeating, at least in the same Lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T14:06:19-07:00","id":1544868,"title":"","content":"One interesting dichotomy that I noticed were the Heirs in contrast to the Premier. The Heirs have bleed one fewer CD for psychic spells - which includes many of the spells that you would expect them to use and that they have access to. The Premier, in the other hand, bleed one fewer CD for liminal spells which they basically have no access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}